State of Kentucky } S.S. County of Allen }
On this 12 th day of August A.D. 1868. Before me John B. Collins, clerk of the county court, a court of record, within and for said county, personally appeared Mrs. Martha Giles, a resident of said county, aged about 113 years, to me personally known, who being by me first duly sworn according to law, doth, on her oath, make the following declaration in order to obtain the benefit of the Joint resolution of Congress of February 18, 1867, granting increased rate of pension to certain widows of soldiers and others of the revolutionary war.
That she is the widow of John Giles, who, was a soldier in said war from near its commencement until its termination, as she well remembers, but as to the particular service he rendered throughout said war she is unable to state, or the names of the officers under whom he served, but he enlisted as a private in said service in the county of Rowan in the State of North Carolina, and for and on account of his said services, he applied for and obtained a pension until his death, which occurred in this Allen county on or about the 12 th day of September 1852, and that she was married to the said John Giles in the county of Rowan in the State of North Carolina by one George Read a Justice of the Peace, but a short time before her said husband enlisted in the service aforesaid, but does not em remember the date of her said marriage, and has no record of it, and for the proof of her said husband's service in said revolutionary war, and her inter-marriage with him, and when it took place, she hereby refers to the papers on file in her original application for a pension, and those filed in the application of her deceased husband, and she further declares, that she is the same person in whose favor a certificate of pension was issued on the 7 th day of August A.D. 1855, by the secretary of the Interior, at the rate of Eighty dollars per annum, commencing on the 12 th day of September 1852, and which pension has been paid her to
